```java
String sql = "SELECT name FROM users WHERE id = ?";
try (Connection con = dataSource.getConnection();
     PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement(sql)) {
    ps.setLong(1, userId);                 // bound param -> no injection
    try (ResultSet rs = ps.executeQuery()) {
        return rs.next() ? rs.getString("name") : null;
    }
}
// rs closes first, then ps, then con -- all returned to the pool, always.
```
*Even if `executeQuery()` throws, every resource is closed and the connection returns to the pool.*

```java
static class Faulty implements AutoCloseable {
    public void work() { throw new RuntimeException("primary: work failed"); }
    public void close() { throw new RuntimeException("suppressed: close failed"); }
}

public static void main(String[] args) {
    try (Faulty f = new Faulty()) {
        f.work();                        // throws primary
    } catch (RuntimeException e) {
        System.out.println(e.getMessage());              // primary: work failed
        for (Throwable s : e.getSuppressed()) {
            System.out.println("  " + s.getMessage());   // suppressed: close failed
        }
    }
}
```
*The body's exception is primary; the `close()` failure is preserved as suppressed, not lost.*
